      "title": "Alkaline hydrolysis of nitriles",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "2d720c54-503b-58ec-b5b1-3307f222f40c",
          "pdf_from": 127,
          "pdf_to": 127,
          "note": "Alkaline hydrolysis of nitriles: a main subheading of 24.4 Alkanenitriles, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 127-127."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "When a nitrile is heated with a dilute sodium hydroxide solution, a salt of carboxylic acid is produced, which on acidification with dilute hydrochloric acid gives free carboxylic acid."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3CN_{(aq)} + H2O_{(l)} + NaOH_{(aq)} -> CH3COONa_{(aq)} + NH3_{(g)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃CN(aq) + H₂O(l) + NaOH(aq) → CH₃COONa(aq) + NH₃(g)"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3COONa_{(aq)} + HCl_{(aq)} -> CH3COOH_{(aq)} + NaCl_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃COONa(aq) + HCl(aq) → CH₃COOH(aq) + NaCl(aq)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
